# What NOT to send to Docker when building the frontend image.
#
# The build context is this folder, and `docker build` uploads all of it to the
# Docker daemon before the first instruction runs. Without this file that
# includes several hundred megabytes of node_modules and build caches.
#
# Speed is the least important reason. The other two matter more.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# node_modules - excluded for CORRECTNESS, not size
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# It holds compiled binaries for the platform it was installed on, such as
# @esbuild/win32-x64. The image is Linux. Copying Windows binaries in makes the
# build fail with an error that reads like a broken dependency and is actually
# a Dockerfile mistake.
#
# The image runs `npm ci` itself, from package-lock.json, so it installs the
# correct Linux binaries. Never ship build artifacts into an image; regenerate
# them there.
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output and caches - rebuilt inside the image
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Your local dist/ is whatever you last built by hand. The image builds its own.
# Excluding it makes that impossible to get wrong. .angular/ is the CLI's local
# build cache.
dist/
.angular/
coverage/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets - a file copied into a layer stays in that layer forever
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deleting it in a later instruction only hides it; `docker history` still has
# it. Keep it out of the context in the first place.
.env
.env.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed to build the bundle
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Excluded so that editing a note does not invalidate the COPY layer and force
# a full rebuild.
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
